model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Accounts and pool displays follow committed scoped revisions through the existing app-data supervisor transport. Hosted account, observation, link, group, role, sharing and session writers record revisions and pending delivery in their SQL transaction. App-source connection enabled state, selection payloads and revocations invalidate account and app projections, including encrypted payload writes without a row revision bump. Reporting, driver-check and execution-target state invalidate account projections; reporting leases alone do not. Home readings and request history map to the actual pool app ID; derived usage, capacity, limit and price changes record their revisions and pending delivery with the runtime adapter source commit. Identical writes and collection bookkeeping do not create revisions, and retry discovery adds no statement to unchanged pool upkeep. Registration precedes the authoritative handshake. A browser accepts a body only between matching current revision reads under one opaque principal/session identity, rejects older in-flight work, and clears protected data on denial. Overview usage, personal usage and capacity publish independently only after their own revision fences; a combined capacity verdict requires matching accepted head versions within one refresh. A slow capacity response never holds usage or its retry. A fresh pool view starts its source read after the caller revision baseline and reloads process-local group metadata that another Home writer may have changed. Authority changes replace paged history and invalidate old pagination; observation freshness expires locally from original source deadlines. Hidden views do no data reads; reconnect compares durable heads and semantic expiry deadlines. An absolute session deadline rechecks authority once and resyncs renewed sessions; heartbeat frames perform no database reads. Current accepted data remains visible only while an actual refresh is in flight or with its original observation and failure state. Unconverted app-version and generic-query reconciliation timers remain in place. A delivery pass has one interruptible ten-second budget, below the fifteen-second process stop allowance. Interrupted SDK and recovery work starts no delivery. Unacknowledged rows survive shutdown and the next process can reacquire the data lock and deliver them. Both hosted and self-hosted transports obey the same contract."
    }
  }
}
